      "trigger": "The operator or another process edits the checker/schema or switches the harness checkout while the container review is running.",
      "execution_path": "establish_trusted_main verifies the checkout before launching Codex. After the potentially 1800-second review, _execute_inspection checks the PR's remote head but directly executes checker_argv, which points to REPO_ROOT/tests/codex_report_status.py. It never repeats audit_inputs or compares the recorded hashes. Cross-grading occurs only when the reviewed PR changed an audited input.",
      "consequence": "A different checker can grade the report while provenance still claims trusted main. Switching the checkout to an untrusted branch can execute that branch's Python on the host; even an ordinary concurrent edit can produce completion under unrecorded grading rules.",
      "evidence": "The trusted _execute_reserved path explicitly re-audits and compares inputs immediately before grading; the new inspection path omits that safeguard. Plan 85.1-06 explicitly requests the same re-audit. An in-memory orchestration check confirmed that the checkout checker is invoked after simulated state change without calling audit_inputs. Existing orchestration tests mock provenance and checker output but do not mutate audited inputs during review.",
